    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0219" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg213"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the identic note which it
                    is proposed that the Governments of Great Britain and of the United States
                    should address to the maritime powers inviting their adhesion to the Bering Sea
                    regulations, I have the honor to submit for your consideration the accompanying
                    list of powers to whom it is suggested by my Government that the identic note
                    should be addressed. I should be glad to be informed whether the list meets with
                    the approval of your Government, and, if so, of the date on which you would
                    propose that the identic note should be issued.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d224-a1.xml" xpointer="d224-a1"/>
